DREAM macOS port: fix VCB11 virtual codebook selection in faac 1.28 DRM mode.

Upstream: https://github.com/knik0/faac tag faac1_28 (065f22740d34437fa74805a32008674d0a9b64e7)
Applies with: git apply faac-1.28-drm-vcb11.patch   (run inside the faac 1.28 tree)

DRM uses the ER "virtual codebooks for codebook 11" (VCB11, codebooks 16..31),
each with a largest absolute value (LAV) of 15, 31, 47, ..., 2047. faac 1.28
chose the codebook by comparing the escape *bit pattern* against those limits,
so e.g. a section whose largest value is 16..31 was signalled as codebook 16
(LAV 15). faad2 does not check LAV and decodes it; fdk-aac's HCR decoder
detects the violation and silences the spectral lines (no error reported),
which showed up as heavy drop-outs at 12 kHz / >= 15 kbit/s per channel.
Now the largest absolute quantised value of the section is compared.
The bitstream size is unchanged (VCB11 books share codebook 11's tables).

diff --git a/libfaac/huffman.c b/libfaac/huffman.c
index 585fd73..b74ee2c 100644
--- a/libfaac/huffman.c
+++ b/libfaac/huffman.c
@@ -783,8 +783,9 @@ int OutputBits(CoderInfo *coderInfo,
                 num_data[coderInfo->cur_cw]++;
                 cur_cw_len += len_esc;
 
-                if (esc_sequence > max_esc_sequ)
-                    max_esc_sequ = esc_sequence;
+                /* VCB11 limits are on the absolute value, not on the escape bit pattern */
+                if (ABS(quant[i]) > max_esc_sequ)
+                    max_esc_sequ = ABS(quant[i]);
 #endif
 
                 /* then code and transmit the second escape_sequence */
@@ -796,8 +797,8 @@ int OutputBits(CoderInfo *coderInfo,
                 num_data[coderInfo->cur_cw]++;
                 cur_cw_len += len_esc;
 
-                if (esc_sequence > max_esc_sequ)
-                    max_esc_sequ = esc_sequence;
+                if (ABS(quant[i+1]) > max_esc_sequ)
+                    max_esc_sequ = ABS(quant[i+1]);
 #endif
             }
             else if (ABS(quant[i]) >= 16) {  /* the first codeword was above 16, not the second one */
@@ -810,8 +811,8 @@ int OutputBits(CoderInfo *coderInfo,
                 num_data[coderInfo->cur_cw]++;
                 cur_cw_len += len_esc;
 
-                if (esc_sequence > max_esc_sequ)
